// Measured: my rebuilt toy LM head (NumPy 2.5.3, CPU, simulated BF16 and FP16 by
// round-to-nearest-even), vocabulary 2,048 (Zipf 1.1), width 64, frozen
// RMS-normalised trunk with a shared mean direction, batch 128, clip 1, 200-step
// warmup. Eval on a fixed held-out batch of 2,048 positions. Scripts kept out of
// the tree. Values rounded to 3-4 significant digits.
//
// INJ_*: SGD-M head (momentum 0.99, lr 0.03). From step 10,000 a fixed vector
// along the mean hidden direction is added to every row of E each step (x1 moves
// the mean logit by about -0.025 a step). gap = native eval loss minus the eval
// loss of the same weights through an FP32 head (clipped at 0 for the log axis).
//
// RATIO_*: per logged eval, r = |mean logit| / std of logits and
// e = RMS(z_native - z_fp32) / std, as in the paper's Figure 18. THEORY rounds
// Gaussian logits shifted to r once, output rounding only.

